      <data key="e_from_type">Document</data>
      <data key="e_to_type">SAPProduct</data>
      <data key="e_source_id">doc:docs/ref-arch/RA0013/6-cloud-identity-services-bdc/readme.md</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://architecture.learning.sap.com/docs/ref-arch/2c8491</data>
      <data key="e_source_file">docs/ref-arch/RA0013/6-cloud-identity-services-bdc/readme.md</data>
      <data key="e_source_section">__introduction__</data>
      <data key="e_evidence">This reference architecture proposes a solution to unify access across the client's landscape with SAP Business Data Cloud (BDC), including SAP Analytics Cloud, SAP Datasphere, and SAP Databricks.</data>
      <data key="e_evidence_type">explicit</data>
      <data key="e_confidence">0.85</data>
      <data key="e_repository_commit">591ed640fd7889503240d282107995a29b075876</data>
      <data key="e_extraction_date">2026-07-15T03:09:16.238251+00:00</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="rel:doc:2c8491:MENTIONS:entity:sap-s4hana:2ada8cd38a" source="doc:2c8491" target="entity:sap-s4hana">
      <data key="e_type">MENTIONS</data>
      <data key="e_from_id">doc:2c8491</data>
      <data key="e_to_id">entity:sap-s4hana</data>
      <data key="e_from_type">Document</data>
      <data key="e_to_type">SAPProduct</data>
      <data key="e_source_id">doc:docs/ref-arch/RA0013/6-cloud-identity-services-bdc/readme.md</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://architecture.learning.sap.com/docs/ref-arch/2c8491</data>
      <data key="e_source_file">docs/ref-arch/RA0013/6-cloud-identity-services-bdc/readme.md</data>
      <data key="e_source_section">Architecture</data>
      <data key="e_evidence">It unifies access by connecting to an authoritative source of truth, which can be an Enterprise IdP or a core business system like **SAP SuccessFactors** (for employee lifecycle) or **SAP S/4HANA** (identity data or business roles).</data>
      <data key="e_evidence_type">explicit</data>
      <data key="e_confidence">0.85</data>
      <data key="e_repository_commit">591ed640fd7889503240d282107995a29b075876</data>
      <data key="e_extraction_date">2026-07-15T03:09:16.238251+00:00</data>
    </edge>
    <edge id="rel:doc:2c8491:MENTIONS:entity:sap-cloud-identity-services:2ada8cd38a" source="doc:2c8491" target="entity:sap-cloud-identity-services">
      <data key="e_type">MENTIONS</data>
      <data key="e_from_id">doc:2c8491</data>
      <data key="e_to_id">entity:sap-cloud-identity-services</data>
      <data key="e_from_type">Document</data>
      <data key="e_to_type">IdentitySecurity</data>
      <data key="e_source_id">doc:docs/ref-arch/RA0013/6-cloud-identity-services-bdc/readme.md</data>
      <data key="e_source_url">https://architecture.learning.sap.com/docs/ref-arch/2c8491</data>
      <data key="e_source_file">docs/ref-arch/RA0013/6-cloud-identity-services-bdc/readme.md</data>
      <data key="e_source_section">__introduction__</data>
      <data key="e_evidence">By leveraging **SAP Cloud Identity Services (CIS)**—including IAS for SSO and IPS for provisioning—you can establish a single source of truth for user identities, groups of access, streamline access control, and enhance security.</data>
      <data key="e_evidence_type">explicit</data>
